                <pb facs="0596" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.42/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-19T18:00:00+01:00">August 19, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 19—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>207. My 192, August 3, 5 p.m. In reply to my oral inquiries made on their behalf,
                    I am informed by the Foreign Office that Jewish American students who have
                    already resided in Italy for 1 year will be free to continue and complete their
                    university studies.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
